  "newlock": {
   "title": "SPRING LOCK REPAIR",
   "sub": "BROKEN LOCK, NEW WELD",
   "track": "Thunder",
   "text": "Spring lock torn up on your car hauler? This one came in with burnt, torn steel around the bracket and the D-ring. Rust and pitting everywhere. First, we cleaned up the frame with a red pad. So what do you do with a lock this far gone? You take out what's broken. We chiseled the old remnants out of the jagged housing. Then we clamped a new steel plate to the frame rail and fitted the bracket, with a wood block in the lock opening. We ground the weld areas, bolted the bracket on, and welded it in. Smooth beads, a solid new lock. Got a broken spring lock? Bring it by the shop.",
